# .trivyignore
#
# Trivy vulnerability scanner ignore file.
# Format: One CVE ID per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Use this file to suppress known false positives or CVEs that are not
# exploitable in the context of this application.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2023-1234  # Not exploitable — requires local access only
#
# Review and update this file after each Trivy scan run.
# See: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/guide/ignore/vulnerability/
